msgid "SPIFFE Client"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://spiffe.io/[SPIFFE] (Secure Production Identity Framework for "
"Everyone) provides cryptographic workload identities in zero-trust "
"environments.\n"
"The SPIFFE client extension uses the https://github.com/spiffe/spiffe/blob/"
"main/standards/SPIFFE_Workload_API.md[Workload API] to retrieve https://"
"github.com/spiffe/spiffe/blob/main/standards/JWT-SVID.md[JWT-SVIDs] and "
"https://github.com/spiffe/spiffe/blob/main/standards/X509-SVID.md[X.509-"
"SVIDs] for Quarkus workloads directly from the local https://spiffe.io/docs/"
"latest/spire-about/spire-concepts/[SPIRE Agent].\n"
"It simplifies deployment by eliminating the need for a SPIFFE client sidecar "
"that stores SVIDs on a mounted file path for Quarkus to read."
msgstr ""

msgid "This technology is considered {extension-status}."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In _experimental_ mode, early feedback is requested to mature the idea.\n"
"There is no guarantee of stability nor long term presence in the platform "
"until the solution matures.\n"
"Feedback is welcome on our https://groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-"
"dev[mailing list] or as issues in our https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"issues[GitHub issue tracker]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a full list of possible statuses, check our https://quarkus.io/faq/#what-"
"are-the-extension-statuses[FAQ entry]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Adding the extension"
msgstr ""

msgid "Add the `quarkus-spiffe-client` extension to your project:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The extension requires the URI of the SPIRE Agent's Workload Endpoint socket:"
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If `quarkus.spiffe-client.endpoint-socket` is not set, the extension falls "
"back to the standard `SPIFFE_ENDPOINT_SOCKET` environment variable as "
"defined by the https://spiffe.io/docs/latest/spiffe-specs/"
"spiffe_workload_endpoint/#4-locating-the-endpoint[SPIFFE Workload Endpoint "
"specification].\n"
"This environment variable is typically set by the SPIRE Agent for workloads "
"it manages."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The URI must use one of the following schemes, as defined by the https://"
"github.com/spiffe/spiffe/blob/main/standards/SPIFFE_Workload_Endpoint."
"md[SPIFFE Workload Endpoint] specification:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`unix://` for Unix Domain Sockets (production default), for example `unix:///"
"run/spire/sockets/agent.sock`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`tcp://` for TCP connections (development and testing), for example `tcp://"
"127.0.0.1:8080`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For the `tcp` scheme, the host must be an IP address and a port is required.\n"
"Hostnames are not accepted."
msgstr ""

msgid "On Windows, only the `tcp://` scheme is currently supported."
msgstr ""

